{#
  BeMart Shopping shipping page — EC-CUBE goShoppingShipping.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Shopping/shipping.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Shopping/shipping.twig).

  DATA page (radio list of registered shipping addresses) — see
  var/templates/README.md. Markup skeleton, the `ec-role` /
  `ec-pageHeader` / `ec-registerRole` / `ec-off1Grid` / `ec-addressRole` /
  `ec-addressList` / `ec-registerRole__actions` classes and the block
  structure are kept verbatim from EC-CUBE.

  EC-CUBE renders one `<input type="radio">` per address inside a
  `{% for choice in form.addresses.vars.choices %}` loop. The address
  set is NOT a free-text form — it is a fixed radio list of the
  customer's already-registered addresses — so the port renders the
  radios as plain markup driven by the body's `addresses` list (the
  data-page recipe), not through a form object.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}` -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `form._token` — Symfony CSRF widget; kept as the hidden `_token`
     input bound to the body's `csrfToken` (null in the html context).
   - `Customer.CustomerAddresses|length < eccube_config.eccube_deliv_
     addr_max` — the over-limit warning is gated on a count the body
     does not carry. The body's `addresses` list is empty (a Wave-future
     TODO — see src/Resource/Page/Shopping/Shipping.php), which is below
     any limit, so the port renders the add-new-address branch (the
     common case). The over-limit warning branch is OMITTED.
   - `has_errors(form.addresses)` — request-validation runtime; resolves
     false on a fresh page, so the unselected-address warning is OMITTED.

  MISSING BODY FIELD follow-up: the authenticated customer's registered
  shipping-address list (`addresses` is empty). With no addresses the
  `{% for %}` radio loop emits nothing — exactly the empty
  `ec-addressList` skeleton. Surfacing the address book is a dedicated
  vertical-slice (AddressStorage scoped to the session), tracked in the
  enrichment backlog.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set body_class = 'other_page' %}
{% set route = 'shopping_shipping' %}
{% set title = 'お届け先の指定' %}

{% block main %}
    <div class="ec-role">
        <div class="ec-pageHeader">
            <h1>お届け先の指定</h1>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ec-registerRole">
        <div class="ec-off1Grid">
            <div class="ec-off1Grid__cell">
                <div class="ec-addressRole">
                    <div class="ec-addressRole__actions"><a class="ec-inlineBtn" href="{{ url('shopping_shipping_edit') }}">新規お届け先を追加する</a></div>
                </div>

                <form method="post" action="{{ url('shopping_shipping') }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken|default('') }}">
                    <div class="ec-addressList">
                        {% for address in addresses %}
                        <div class="ec-addressList__item">
                            <div class="ec-addressList__remove">
                                <input type="radio" id="address{{ address.id }}" name="address" value="{{ address.id }}" />
                            </div>
                            <div class="ec-addressList__address">
                                <div>{{ address.name01 }}&nbsp;{{ address.name02 }}</div>
                                <div>〒{{ address.postalCode }} {{ address.pref }}{{ address.addr01 }}{{ address.addr02 }}</div>
                                <div>{{ address.phoneNumber }}</div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>

                    <div class="ec-registerRole__actions">
                        <div class="ec-off4Grid">
                            <div class="ec-off4Grid__cell">
                                <button type="submit" class="ec-blockBtn--action">選択したお届け先に送る</button>
                                <a class="ec-blockBtn--cancel" href="{{ url('shopping') }}">戻る</a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </form>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>
{% endblock %}
